# Hatchery Core

Windows-first VM manager; **Hatchery Controller** (Controller plane) runs on Linux / macOS / Windows; **Nests** (Nest plane) are libvirt / UTM / Hyper-V (**Local Nest** or **Remote Nest**). See `.hatchery/docs/architecture-nests.md` and epic #202. v1 guests: Win10, Win11, Server 2022/2025.

## Naming (1:1:1 — UI, docs, code)

Use Hatchery terms where they clarify product concepts. Prefer **clear, universal** lifecycle words in the UI. Never invent synonyms. Never use retired "Brood". Avoid “host” in product copy — say **Controller** or **Nest**.

| Term | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Hatchery Controller** (Controller for short) | Device where the Hatchery UI runs; responsible for controlling the Nest(s) |
| **Nest** | Hypervisor the Controller communicates with to manage guest VMs |
| **Local Nest** | Nest on the same device as the Controller (Controller also manages guest VMs on that device) |
| **Remote Nest** | Nest the Controller reaches across the control plane to manage guest VMs |

| Use | Not |
|---|---|
| Clutch | stack / blueprint / compose file |
| Hatch | deploy / provision (for create+boot) |
| Cull | destroy / delete / terminate (VM remove) |
| Snapshot | Freeze (retired brand verb) |
| Revert (to snapshot) | Thaw (retired brand verb) |
| Delete snapshot | — |
| Health check / connectivity check | Chirp (retired as primary UI label) |
| Fledged | ready / healthy (post-provision) |

Power actions stay plain: Start, Stop, Force Stop, Pause, Resume.

```
❌ "Delete the VM and remove its disk"
✅ "Cull the VM"

❌ "Freeze" / "Thaw" / "Chirp" as primary button labels
✅ Snapshot / Revert / Delete snapshot; "Test Nest connection" or "Guest health check"

❌ create_snapshot_blueprint()
✅ Follow existing provider names (create_snapshot / revert_snapshot / delete_snapshot)
```

Provider method names already use snapshot language — keep them. Do not rename code to Freeze/Thaw.
## Design constraints

- Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS only — no JS framework
- Hypervisor differences stay in `lib/providers/`
- Answer files and provisioning adapt to guest OS — do not assume Windows everywhere
- Surface errors in the UI, not only logs
- Prefer editing existing files; no new abstraction layers beyond the task
- Project meta belongs in `.hatchery/` (not required to run the app)
- No devcontainers — Local Nest libvirt/KVM still needs a real Nest environment when used
- **Consumer distribution north star ([#273](https://github.com/dustinestes/Hatchery/issues/273)):** OS package managers install **Controller only** (empty Nest registry); Nest setup is docs + validators. Contributor paths may keep `uv` / gunicorn for development and tests.

When adding VM features, read `lib/providers/base.py` before extending the provider interface.

Human docs: `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `README.md`, `.hatchery/docs/`.
